course: dictionary
lesson: 14619
title: One word, three meanings: portal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word portal can mean a grand doorway, a magic doorway into another world, or a website that is the starting point for a service. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «The huge stone portal of the cathedral was carved with saints and angels.» Huge, stone and carved tell you it is a grand entrance to a building. Here portal means a grand doorway.
explain: «Mia pushed the glowing door and stepped through the portal into a land of talking foxes.» Glowing and talking foxes tell you the portal is magic, a doorway into another world.
explain: «Every morning, Sam logs in to the school learning portal to find his homework.» Logging in and finding homework tell you that here a portal is a website. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, swap each meaning into the sentence and pick the one that still makes sense.
fact: A portal is a doorway or entrance.
fact: «Portal» can mean a large, grand doorway or entrance to a building.
fact: In stories and games, a portal is a magic doorway that takes you to another world or place.
fact: On a computer, a portal is a website that is the starting point for a service, such as a school login page.
fact: Clue words such as «magic», «carved», or «logs in» show you which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The knight walked through the castle portal, its arch carved with birds.» What does portal mean here? | *A grand doorway into a building | A school login page | A kind of small boat | A magic doorway to another world
exercise: «The portal glowed purple, and Max vanished into a world of floating islands.» What kind of portal is this? | A grand stone doorway | *A magic doorway to another world | A website for homework | A type of petrol station
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Log in to the parent portal to see your child's marks.» What does portal mean? | A magic doorway | A stone arch on an old church | *A website that is the starting point for a service | A large doorway for trains
test: «Ella stepped into the portal and the grey city vanished in a flash of light.» What does portal mean? | *A magic doorway to another world | A school login page | A grand stone arch on a cathedral | A tall tower with a bell
test: Which sentence uses portal to mean a website? | «The huge oak portal was twice as tall as the door.» | *«Ben logged in to the learning portal to do his maths.» | «The portal opened and a dragon flew out.» | «He ran through the portal into the wild night.»
exam: What does the word portal mean in «The cathedral's west portal was carved with saints»? | *A grand stone doorway | A school login page | A tall tower with a bell | A magic doorway to another world
